President Trump Renames AI as SI, Tech Leaders Address Super Intelligence Safety

President Donald Trump announced that the executive branch would replace the term “Artificial Intelligence” with “Super Intelligence,” while joining technology executives to discuss an industry accord addressing the development and safety of the technology.
A White House fact sheet released September 29 said Trump signed an executive order directing the terminology change across the executive branch. The administration described the decision as recognition of the advancing technological frontier and the opportunities it could offer Americans.

